{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1250408-dramatic-failure","id":1250408,"title":"Dramatic failure","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-31T23:19:22-07:00","id":1250408,"title":"Dramatic failure","content":"How does one determine a failure from a dramatic failure? I mean like I look at vampire disciplines and am not exactly sure what the target number for successes is even. Anyone care to enlighten me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T23:29:55-07:00","id":1250410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThriceHonored</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1250408-dramatic-failure#post1250408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one determine a failure from a dramatic failure? I mean like I look at vampire disciplines and am not exactly sure what the target number for successes is even. Anyone care to enlighten me?</div> </div> </div> </div>A dramatic failure results most directly from rolling a 1 on the die you roll when you have an effective dice pool size of 0 or less; that same die treats everything else except a 10 as a failure, unlike the normal roll results of &quot;any die that comes up 7 or less is a failure, any die that comes up 8 or more is a success.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T00:05:51-07:00","id":1250411,"title":"","content":"In 2e era games, players can also choose to have a normal failure to become a dramatic failure for a Beat. Some Conditions can also have the same effect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T00:31:17-07:00","id":1250415,"title":"","content":"The target number on a die is 8 and above, with exploding 10s. If you mean the number of successful dice rolled, there typically isn\u2019t a threshold; the quantity of the successes usually doesn\u2019t matter unless the roll is contested, or the action is combat-based, although rolling 5 successes is considered an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> Dramatic failure occurs:<br /> <br /> A) when the player chooses to downgrade a regular failure to a dramatic one for a Beat, or<br /> <br /> B) if the player rolls a 1 on a Chance Die, which is a single die one can roll even if a dice pool is reduced to 0 or below, due to negative modifiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 09-01-2018, 03:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T08:30:42-07:00","id":1250456,"title":"","content":"The target number of successes for a roll that isn't contested by an opposing roll is one. If you get one success, your action succeeds, period. Difficulty is imposed by circumstantial dice penalties. A die rolls a success on an eight or above, which is relatively swingy, so requiring more than one success would yield a pretty high rate of failure for even well trained dice pools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 09-01-2018, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T10:42:27-07:00","id":1250482,"title":"","content":"I must admit that I love the notion of taking a Beat to downgrade a Failure to a Dramatic Failure. Without this, I think I saw two Dramatic Failures in 6+ years of running W/CoD. This not only leads to a lot of more interesting situations, but also gives the players a lot of agency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5435-mhicwombat","name":"MhicWombat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T18:11:18-07:00","id":1250921,"title":"","content":"There are also occasionally supernatural powers that can force dramatic failures. Thief of Fate for one example, though the way most work means that it is still pretty unlikely unless they are doing something they arn't particularly good at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}